<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35248" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδοι-άζω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεδοίασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Id.</u>
					2.6
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Gall.</u>
				11
			</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δοιῇ</span>):—<i>to be
				in doubt, at a loss</i>, c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν . . ἐνδοιάζῃ Χωρίον προσλαβεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.36
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐνδοιάζοντες</span> the
				<i>waverers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.91
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲν ἐνδοιάσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Herm.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῇ γνώμῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Sull.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cat. Mi.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Phal.</u>
					2.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εἰ</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				4.58
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of things, 
			<i>to be matter of doubt</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγῳ ἐνδοιασθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.122
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδοιαζόμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					7.59
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.622
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεδοιάζετο δὲ πότερον</span>
			. . <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				2.21
			</span></i>: aor. 1 also in act. sense, <i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				9.6
			</span></i>.</div>
